      "answer": "$r=2$, $\\theta=0.5$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Perimeter $=r+r\\theta+r+2r\\times2\\theta+r+r\\theta+r=4r+6r\\theta$ — B1\nArea $=\\dfrac12r^2\\theta+\\dfrac12(2r)^2(2\\theta)+\\dfrac12r^2\\theta=5r^2\\theta$ — B1\n$4r+6r\\theta=14$ and $5r^2\\theta=10$ — M1*; equations $ar+br\\theta=14$ and $cr^2\\theta=10$, where $a,b,c\\neq0$; terms may be uncollected.\nEliminate $\\theta$: $5r^2\\dfrac{14-4r}{6r}=10$ or $4r+6r(\\dfrac{10}{5r^2})=14$ — DM1; obtain an equation in $r$.\n$2r^2-7r+6=0\\Rightarrow(r-2)(2r-3)=0$ — DM1; factorise or another accepted method for their three-term quadratic.\nAlternative elimination: $5(\\dfrac{14}{4+6\\theta})^2\\theta=10$ or $4\\sqrt{\\dfrac{10}{5\\theta}}+6\\sqrt{\\dfrac{10}{5\\theta}}\\theta=14$ — DM1; obtain an equation in $\\theta$.\n$18\\theta^2-25\\theta+8=0\\Rightarrow(9\\theta-8)(2\\theta-1)=0$ — DM1; factorise or another accepted method for their three-term quadratic.\n$r=2$ and $\\theta=0.5$ — B1; condone extra answers $r=\\dfrac32$ and $\\theta=\\dfrac89$.\nTotal: 6",
